# Legacy peer-deps resolution.
#
# Original (May 2026) reason — superseded, kept for historical context:
#   apps/mobile pulled react-native@0.85 which peers react@^19, while the
#   workspace pinned react@^18.3 (web + api expected 18). React@19 upgrade
#   was tracked in PRs #471 + #467; that pair is now MERGED and react@19
#   + react-dom@19 are pinned across web + mobile.
#
# Current (post-#471/#467) reason — STILL REQUIRED:
#   2026-05-05 evening reviewer pass attempted to delete this file. `npm
#   install` immediately tripped ERESOLVE on a NEW conflict shape: the
#   apps/mobile/node_modules/react-dom subtree still contains the legacy
#   18.3.1 entries from before the react@19 bump (the lockfile reorg that
#   came with #471/#467 didn't fully replace transitive react-dom in the
#   mobile workspace tree). With strict peer-deps mode, npm refuses to
#   reconcile the declared `react-dom@^19.2.5` against the resident 18.3.1.
#
# Fix path to fully retire this flag:
#   1. `cd apps/mobile && rm -rf node_modules` (force a fresh resolve)
#   2. `cd <repo root> && rm -rf node_modules package-lock.json && npm install`
#      WITHOUT `legacy-peer-deps=true` (delete this file first)
#   3. If install passes -> commit the regenerated lockfile + delete this .npmrc
#   4. If install fails -> restore this .npmrc and document the new conflict
#
# This is a CI-impacting change (touches lockfile shape); do it as a
# dedicated PR with a clean rebase against main, not bundled with feature
# work.
legacy-peer-deps=true
